/*  Bits — `0xFF`, `0b1010`, the arithmetic and the gates over them, `shifted left by`,
    `converted to hex`, `converted to number`, and a pattern written or set in a text.

    ★ A bits value is the runtime's `CufetBits` — its value, the base it is shown in and its width —
      passed by value. Everything it does is a runtime call `cufet build` makes too, so a result's
      base and width come out of one place for both compilers.

    ★ Two patterns compare on their VALUE alone: `0xFF`, `0x00FF` and `0b11111111` are one pattern
      written three ways, so a width is never what tells two apart.
*/

Pull books on collections, and the c-language.
    /// Whether an expression gives a bits value by what it is, whatever it is made from.
    Bind fact to is-bits-expression, given (the text kind):
        Return kind is "BitsLiteral" or kind is "BitsShift" or kind is "BitsConvert" or kind is "BitsAtWidth".
    Done.

    /// A bits expression as C.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-bits-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        If kind is "BitsLiteral":
            Define c-language bits-made, given (the number pattern, the term base, the number width),
                as [((CufetBits){ UINT64_C(the pattern), 'the base', the width })].
            Return bits-made on (cast line-number on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)), cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)),
                cast line-number on (cast field-of on (expression, 3))).
        Done.
        Define target-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "BitsShift":
            Define c-language bits-shifted, given (the c-language axiom target, the c-language axiom amount, the fact left, the number at-line),
                as [cufet_bits_shift(the target, the amount, the left, the at-line)].
            Define amount-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) or pass the failure off.
            Return bits-shifted on (target-c, amount-c, (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word is "true", cast line-number on (cast field-of on (expression, 4))).
        Done.
        If kind is "BitsConvert":
            Define c-language bits-converted, given (the c-language axiom target, the term base, the number at-line),
                as [cufet_bits_from_number(the target, 'the base', the at-line)].
            Return bits-converted on (target-c, cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)), cast line-number on (cast field-of on (expression, 3))).
        Done.
        Define width-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Return call-at-line on ("cufet_bits_at_width", target-c, width-c, cast line-number on (cast field-of on (expression, 3))).
    Done.

    /// A binary operator over two bits values already as C: arithmetic and the gates give bits —
    /// the gates are calls, not `&&`, since combining two patterns needs both — and a comparison
    /// gives a fact, on the values alone.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-bits-binary, given (the text operator, the c-language axiom left, the c-language axiom right, the number at-line):
        Define c-language value-test, given (the c-language axiom left, the c-language axiom right, the c-language axiom test),
            as [((the left).value the test (the right).value)].
        Judge operator, where it is:
            "Plus", return call-at-line on ("cufet_bits_add", left, right, at-line).
            "Minus", return call-at-line on ("cufet_bits_sub", left, right, at-line).
            "Star", return call-at-line on ("cufet_bits_mul", left, right, at-line).
            "Slash", return call-at-line on ("cufet_bits_div", left, right, at-line).
            "Percent", return call-at-line on ("cufet_bits_mod", left, right, at-line).
            "And", return call-of-two on ("cufet_bits_and", left, right).
            "Or", return call-of-two on ("cufet_bits_or", left, right).
            "Xor", return call-of-two on ("cufet_bits_xor", left, right).
            "Equal", return value-test on (left, right, [==]).
            "NotEqual", return value-test on (left, right, [!=]).
            "Lt", return value-test on (left, right, [<]).
            "Gt", return value-test on (left, right, [>]).
            "Lte", return value-test on (left, right, [<=]).
            "Gte", return value-test on (left, right, [>=]).
            Otherwise, return a failure (cast not-built on ("the operator {operator} on bits")).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// What a binary operator gives when its left side is bits: bits for arithmetic and the
    /// gates, a fact for a comparison.
    Bind text to bits-binary-kind, given (the text operator):
        If operator is "Plus" or operator is "Minus" or operator is "Star" or operator is "Slash" or operator is "Percent"
                or operator is "And" or operator is "Or" or operator is "Xor":
            Return "bits".
        Done.
        Return "fact".
    Done.

    /// A bits value as the text it shows as — `0xFF`, prefix and all — in a buffer of its own.
    Bind c-language axiom to c-bits-text, given (the c-language axiom value):
        Define c-language bits-shown, given (the c-language axiom value),
            as [({ char* cf_bt = (char*)cufet_arena_alloc(80); cufet_format_bits(cf_bt, 80, the value); cf_bt; })].
        Return bits-shown on (value).
    Done.
Done.
